PROJECT — Counter Bug Detection & Repair
counter_buggy.sv
Here we intentionally create an incorrect counter.
module counter_buggy (
    input logic clk,
    input logic rst,
    input logic enable,
    output logic [3:0] count
);

always_ff @(posedge clk) begin

    if (rst)
        count <= 4'd0;

    else if (enable)
        count <= count + 4'd2; // BUG

end

endmodule
The expected behavior is increment by 1, but the defective RTL increments by 2.
4. Formal verification properties
counter_formal.sv
module counter_formal;

    logic clk;
    logic rst;
    logic enable;

    logic [3:0] count;

    counter_buggy dut (
        .clk (clk),
        .rst (rst),
        .enable (enable),
        .count (count)
    );

    initial clk = 0;

    always #1 clk = ~clk;

    // Reset assumption
    initial begin
        rst = 1;
        enable = 0;

        #2;

        rst = 0;
    end

    // Keep enable active for testing
    always @(posedge clk) begin

        if (!rst)
            enable <= 1;

    end

    // Counter must increment by exactly 1
    always @(posedge clk) begin

        if (!rst && enable)
            assert(count == $past(count) + 1);

    end

    // Counter should never exceed 15
    always @(posedge clk) begin

        assert(count <= 15);
        
    end

endmodule
The key idea is that an assert() represents a property the formal solver attempts to falsify; assumptions constrain the legal input space. �
SymbiYosys

5. SymbiYosys configuration
counter.sby
[options]

mode bmc
depth 10


[engines]

smtbmc z3


[script]

read -formal counter_buggy.sv
read -formal counter_formal.sv

prep -top counter_formal


[files]

counter_buggy.sv
counter_formal.sv
Run:
sby -f counter.sby
You should get a FAIL because:
count <= count + 2
does not satisfy:
count == $past(count) + 1
6. Repair the counter
counter_fixed.sv
module counter_fixed (
    input logic clk,
    input logic rst,
    input logic enable,
    output logic [3:0] count
);

always_ff @(posedge clk) begin

    if (rst)
        count <= 4'd0;

    else if (enable)
        count <= count + 4'd1;

end

endmodule
Change the formal file:
counter_fixed dut (
    .clk (clk),
    .rst (rst),
    .enable (enable),
    .count (count)
);
Run again:
sby -f counter.sby
Expected:
PASS
